<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Exclusive Choices
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Radio buttons are appropriate for a small set of mutually exclusive choices that benefits from being visible at the same time. Select a default only when one option is safe and genuinely appropriate for most users.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Provide Group Context
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Place related options in a <Code Tag>RadioGroup</Code> with a clear group label, and give every radio a concise standalone label. Use a <Anchor To="docs/components/select">Select</Anchor> when the list is long or space is constrained, and <Anchor To="docs/components/check">Check</Anchor> components when multiple selections are allowed.
</DocsPageParagraph>

